================================================================================================
(5) anti-order 10 at n = 10: explicit construction (2*mu law upper bound)
================================================================================================
  tournament OK: True ; sigma = tau o r is anti-auto: True ; order(sigma) = 10
  => anti-order 10 realized at n = 10.  Lower bound n >= 10 for order-10:
  sigma^2 = order-5 auto a; an involutive-part tau commuting with a must map
  each 5-orbit to a DIFFERENT 5-orbit (centralizer of a 5-cycle in S5 = Z5 has
  no involution; tau|orbit = id would force an arcless 5-set) => orbits paired
  => n >= 10.  THE 2*mu(m) LAW: minimal n for anti-order 2m = 2*mu(m), mu = 
  minimal degree of an order-m permutation.  m=3: n=6 (census); m=5: n=10 (here);
  m=15: n=16 (predicted, NOT 30: orbits {3,5} paired).
DONE.

